---
import PageShell from '../../../components/PageShell.astro';
import { docLinks } from '../../../data/doc-links';
---

<PageShell title="Service to the University">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      As Biology Curriculum Coordinator, I contribute to the operation and continued development of the Open
      Learning Academy. I have participated in the hiring of ten adjunct faculty members through search
      committee work and subsequently support these faculty through onboarding, course readiness
      communications, term-start webinars, troubleshooting, and ongoing questions related to curriculum and
      course content. I also assist with teaching assignments and communicate with external vendors to
      address issues affecting the delivery of Biology courses.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before each academic term, I provide Biology faculty with course-readiness information and
      expectations and conduct spot checks of courses once the term begins to identify missing or incomplete
      items that could affect student readiness. I have also developed instructional videos explaining the
      self-paced course model and created student-facing guidance to address recurring difficulties with
      third-party laboratory platforms. These efforts are intended to support both faculty and students and
      contribute to a consistent experience across OLA offerings.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also contribute to the Biology Department through regular collaboration with the Biology Chair and
      participation in departmental activities. I meet regularly with the leadership of the department to
      review the progress of online course development and attend Biology Department meetings. My Coordinator
      role has provided a bridge between the Biology Department and the Open Learning Academy, helping
      ensure that online Biology courses reflect departmental academic expectations while also addressing the
      needs of the OLA student population.
    </p>
    <p>
      A significant component of my service has been supporting faculty beyond my own teaching
      responsibilities. I serve as a first point of contact for adjunct faculty regarding curriculum and
      course-content questions, assist faculty in navigating course-development expectations, and provide
      resources to help them successfully develop and teach online courses. I have also contributed to the
      development of a formal adjunct faculty evaluation process based on the Quality Matters framework,
      which we hope to implement in the coming academic year.
    </p>
    <p>
      In order to assist our marketing department and to increase student enrollment via SEO optimization, I
      wrote several articles around our OLA courses that are all published online. Examples of the articles
      can be found <a href={docLinks.olaMarketingArticle} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      In addition, I have contributed to institutional conversations around new academic opportunities,
      including the development of a proposed Post-Baccalaureate Pre-Health Certificate. This work reflects
      my interest in using my experience with online curriculum and post-baccalaureate education to
      contribute to the broader academic mission of the University.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageShell>
